meta {
  name: update self (handle)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

patch {
  url: {{user_url}}/users/{{user_id}}
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "handle": "Alice_Prime"
  }
}

docs {
  Self-service profile edit: expect 200 with the updated user. Absent
  fields keep their value; an empty avatar_url string clears the
  avatar. Because logins fill the profile only at account creation,
  this edit survives every later login.

  handle is the account's single identity now (display_name was
  retired from this endpoint; it only ever seeds the handle at
  upsert-time, never stored). A typed change like this one is
  cooldown-gated (429 handle_cooldown on a repeat within the window)
  and answers 409 handle_taken on a folded-key collision with another
  account.

  Validation answers 400 invalid_body naming the field: a handle
  outside 2-30 characters (alphanumeric plus interior underscores) or
  on the reserved list, or an avatar_url that is not http(s) or is
  over 2048 chars. Editing anyone else (or with a service/admin token)
  answers 403: profiles are self-service only.

  The direct DELETE /users/{id} endpoint deliberately has no flow
  here: deleting the row alone would orphan the account's collection
  data. The orchestrated deletion lives in bff "delete me".
}
